{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Braiding.SlNFramingColourFactor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Braiding.SlNFramingColourFactor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Defs"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.forced_framing_eq_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.forced_framing_eq_inv","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SlNFramingColourFactor.lean#L131-L143","doc":"**Forcing.** With `q = x^N` (`x > 0`) the gl_N monodromy of `V` around\nthe q-antisymmetric line `Λ^N_q V` is `q² = x^(2N)`. A rescaling `σ ↦ cσ`\nmultiplies it by `c^(2N)` (2N crossings). Requiring the colour singlet to\nbraid trivially, `c^(2N) · x^(2N) = 1`, forces the unique positive solution\n`c = x⁻¹ = q^(-1/N)`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:sl-n-color-framing","label":"prop:sl-n-color-framing","md":"quantum-observable-universe/eightfold-way/sl-n-color-framing.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.rescale_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.rescale_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SlNFramingColourFactor.lean#L109-L123","doc":"Rescaling preserves a quadratic Hecke-type relation: if\n`(σ - a)(σ - b) = 0` in an algebra, then `(cσ - ca)(cσ - cb) = 0`.\nThe sl_N generator `q^(-1/N) σ` therefore satisfies a Hecke relation with\neigenvalues `q^(1-1/N)` and `-q^(-1-1/N)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.sl_exponent_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.sl_exponent_sum","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SlNFramingColourFactor.lean#L104-L107","doc":"The sum of the two sl_N log-exponents is `-2/N`, not `0`. The gl_N\ncancellation `|det σ| = 1` is the u₁ shift `2 · (1/N)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.sl_ratio_eq_two_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.sl_ratio_eq_two_iff","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SlNFramingColourFactor.lean#L89-L102","doc":"The sl_N channel ratio `(1 + 1/N)/(1 - 1/N)` equals `2` iff `N = 3`\n(for `N ≠ 0, 1`). In gl_N the same ratio is `1` for every `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.colourFactor_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.colourFactor_three","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SlNFramingColourFactor.lean#L81-L87","doc":"At `N = 3` the colour factors are `+1/3` (sextet) and `-2/3`\n(antitriplet). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.glExp_anti_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.glExp_anti_eq","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SlNFramingColourFactor.lean#L76-L79","doc":"The gl_N (Hecke) antisymmetric exponent `-1` is `2 c_anti + 1/N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.glExp_sym_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.glExp_sym_eq","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SlNFramingColourFactor.lean#L71-L74","doc":"The gl_N (Hecke) symmetric exponent `1` is `2 c_sym + 1/N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.slExp_anti_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.slExp_anti_eq","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SlNFramingColourFactor.lean#L63-L69","doc":"The sl_N antisymmetric exponent `-(1 + 1/N)` is twice the antitriplet\ncolour factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.slExp_sym_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.slExp_sym_eq","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SlNFramingColourFactor.lean#L56-L61","doc":"The sl_N symmetric exponent `1 - 1/N` is twice the sextet colour factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.colourFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.colourFactor","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SlNFramingColourFactor.lean#L52-L54","doc":"One-gluon-exchange colour factor `(C₂(R) - 2 C_F)/2` on a summand `R`\nof `V ⊗ V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.casimirAnti","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.casimirAnti","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SlNFramingColourFactor.lean#L49-L50","doc":"Casimir of `Λ² V`: `(N+1)(N-2)/N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.casimirSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.casimirSym","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SlNFramingColourFactor.lean#L46-L47","doc":"Casimir of `Sym² V`: `(N-1)(N+2)/N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.casimirF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SlNFraming.casimirF","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/SlNFramingColourFactor.lean#L43-L44","doc":"Fundamental Casimir `C_F = (N² - 1)/(2N)` (normalisation `T_F = 1/2`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}